# Backend Conventions

- Express 5 + Mongoose 9, CommonJS modules. Entry point: `server.js`, port 5000.
- Contact/review routes still return 501 (scaffold); MongoDB only connects if
  `MONGO_URI` is set in `.env`. The content/admin API is LIVE and uses no DB.
- Structure: `config/` (db connection), `models/` (Mongoose schemas),
  `routes/` (Express routers mounted under `/api/*` in `server.js`),
  `lib/` (contentStore file persistence), `middleware/` (JWT auth),
  `data/` (content JSON), `scripts/` (hash-password.js).
- Content API: `GET /api/content` (public) reads `data/content.json` (seeded
  from `data/content.default.json` on first run; gitignored, survives deploys);
  `PUT /api/content` (requires `requireAdmin` JWT middleware) validates required
  top-level keys + 200KB cap and writes atomically (tmp file + rename).
- Admin auth: `POST /api/admin/login` bcrypt-compares against
  `ADMIN_PASSWORD_HASH`, signs a 12h JWT with `JWT_SECRET` (both required in
  `.env`, else 503). In-memory rate limit: 5 failed attempts / 15 min / IP.
- Admin images: authenticated `POST /api/admin/coach-images` and
  `POST /api/admin/program-images` accept one JPG/PNG/WebP up to 5MB. Shared
  processing in `lib/imageUpload.js` validates, strips metadata, and writes
  normalized WebP files under `data/uploads/coaches/` (640x800) or
  `data/uploads/programs/` (1200x800). Files are served read-only from
  `/api/uploads/`; the runtime upload directory is gitignored and survives deploys.
- Models: `Review` (has `approved` flag for moderation) and `ContactMessage`
  (has `handled` flag). Both use timestamps and input length limits.
- Environment via `dotenv`; template in `.env.example`. Never commit `.env`.
- When implementing routes: validate/sanitize request bodies at the boundary,
  return JSON errors, and keep public endpoints read-only for approved content.
- Do NOT start the server (`node server.js` / `npm run dev`) — the user runs it.
